<title>NETHERLANDS: IHC CALAND SETS 1996 STOCK DIV AT 1 PER 63.</title>
<headline>IHC CALAND SETS 1996 STOCK DIV AT 1 PER 63.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipbuilding and engineering firm IHC Caland NV said on Wednesday it had set the stock alternative to its 1996 dividend at one new share for every 63 shares already held.</p>
<p>In April, IHC announced it would pay a 1996 cash dividend of 1.80 guilders, up from 1.60 guilders in the previous year. It said at the time that the final payment could be taken up in cash or in new shares.</p>
<p>IHC shares traded at 108.80 guilders on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange on Wednesday, up 0.20 from their previous close.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 (fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
